::: {.doc-subject}

Read a Validate object from disk that was previously saved with `write_file()`.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/pointblank/blob/main/pointblank/validate.py#L757-L922){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
read_file(filepath)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

This function loads a validation object that was previously serialized to disk using the
`write_file()` function. The validation object will be restored with all its validation results,
metadata, and optionally the source data (if it was saved with `keep_tbl=True`).

:::{.callout-warning}
The `read_file()` function is currently experimental. Please report any issues you encounter in
the [Pointblank issue tracker](https://github.com/posit-dev/pointblank/issues).
:::
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[filepath]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Path]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The path to the saved validation file. Can be a string or Path object.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Validate]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The restored validation object with all its original state, validation results, and
    metadata.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}



Let's first save a validation object to disk with `write_file()`. We'll use a temporary
directory here, and `keep_tbl=True` saves the target table along with the validation results:

::: {#223213c9 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pointblank as pb
import os
import tempfile

validation = (
    pb.Validate(data=pb.load_dataset("small_table"), tbl_name="small_table")
    .col_vals_gt(columns="d", value=1000)
    .col_vals_not_null(columns="c")
    .interrogate()
)

save_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp()
pb.write_file(validation, "my_validation", path=save_dir, keep_tbl=True, quiet=True)
```
:::


Now we can load the validation object from disk with `read_file()`. The filename can be given
without its extension, in which case `read_file()` looks for `"my_validation.pkl"`:

::: {#1cf1d676 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
restored = pb.read_file(os.path.join(save_dir, "my_validation"))

restored
```

